# The patches are applied by GNU patch against sources extracted from the
# pinned tarball, which uses LF throughout. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true and would rewrite these files to CRLF on checkout, leaving
# every context line with a trailing CR: hunks then apply "with fuzz", meaning
# patch guessed at the location, or fail outright. Pin them.
*.patch text eol=lf

# Verification and build scripts run under bash, which does not tolerate CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
